    {
      "text": "offer the gift … for a testimony, Matt. 8:4 (Mark 1:44; Luke 5:14). brought before governors and kings … for a testimony against them, Matt. 10:18 (Mark 13:9; Luke 21:13). Thou art the Christ, Matt. 16:16 (Luke 9:20). flesh and blood hath not revealed it unto thee, Matt. 16:17. shake off the dust … for a testimony against, Mark 6:11 (Luke 9:5; D&C 75:20). I saw, and bare record that this is the Son, John 1:34 (1:7, 15). I receive not testimony from man, John 5:34. do his will … shall know of the doctrine, John 7:17. law, that the testimony of two men is true, John 8:17. ye shall know the truth, John 8:32. life eternal, that they might know thee the only true God, John 17:3. we know that his testimony is true, John 21:24. gave testimony unto the word of his grace, Acts 14:3. they will not receive thy testimony concerning me, Acts 22:18. testimony of Christ was confirmed in you, 1 Cor. 1:6. declaring unto you the testimony of God, 1 Cor. 2:1. say that Jesus is the Lord, but by the Holy Ghost, 1 Cor. 12:3. testimony of our conscience, 2 Cor. 1:12. received it … by the revelation of Jesus Christ, Gal. 1:12. our testimony among you was believed, 2 Thes. 1:10. Be not … ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, 2 Tim. 1:8. before his translation he had this testimony, Heb. 11:5. Whosoever shall confess that Jesus is the Son, 1 Jn. 4:15. He that believeth … hath the witness in himself, 1 Jn. 5:10. Who bare record … of the testimony of Jesus Christ, Rev. 1:2. slain … for the testimony which they held, Rev. 6:9. overcame him … by the word of their testimony, Rev. 12:11. temple of the tabernacle of the testimony, Rev. 15:5. testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy, Rev. 19:10.",
